ely based on Mac sales.\nTwenty years later, Apple is a completely different company.&\nAs this chart from Statista shows, the percentage of Apple's revenue attributable to Mac computer sales has steadily decline over the last two decades, shrinking to roughly one tenth of total sales last year.&\nApple's Mac sales have actually increased year-over-year, with only a few marginal dips in the last two decades. But that steady growth pales in comparison to the growth provided by a succession of new hit products, from the iPod to the iPhone. Since 2000, sales revenue from Macs almost quadrupled but Apple's total sales revenue multiplied by tens of thousands, as the company released device after device and grew its app store. With almost every product release, the Mac's contribution to the top line diminished.&\nSEE ALSO:& Silicon Valley's pay gap between women and men in tech is so wide it increases the national average\n What Trump University was really like — according to a former professor", "external_links": ["http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?i=o15zSy5kcFA:uQE6b9BnDlE:gIN9vFwOqvQ", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?d=bcOpcFrp8Mo", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?a=o15zSy5kcFA:uQE6b9BnDlE:cGdyc7Q-1BI", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?a=o15zSy5kcFA:uQE6b9BnDlE:gIN9vFwOqvQ", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?a=o15zSy5kcFA:uQE6b9BnDlE:bcOpcFrp8Mo", "http://www.businessinsider.com/silicon-valley-pay-gap-lower-national-average-2018-5", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?d=QXVau8BzmBE", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?d=cGdyc7Q-1BI", "http://feeds.feedburner.com/~ff/typepad/alleyinsider/silicon_alley_insider?i=o15zSy5kcFA:uQE6b9BnDlE:V_sGLiPBpWU", "http://www.businessinsider.com/